      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "content": "### EWMA alpha comparison test\n\nRun `run-ewma-alpha-comparison.ps1`. The script runs the same traffic scenario for each alpha in sequence (default: **0.2, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7**) and restarts only `pacing-api` between runs. Prometheus keeps the historical samples, while the `ewma_alpha` label keeps the runs separated.\n\n**Scenario**\n- Warmup: 50 RPS for 60s\n- Spike: 300 RPS for 60s\n- Recovery: 50 RPS for 90s\n\n**How to choose alpha**\n1. Check how quickly the EWMA observed RPS follows the 300 RPS spike.\n2. Check how quickly it falls back after recovery.\n3. Check whether the applied PASS rate oscillates unnecessarily.\n4. Prefer the smallest alpha that reacts fast enough without excessive oscillation.\n\nThe dashboard is intentionally based on `ewma_alpha`, not campaign ID, so the comparison does not create high-cardinality campaign-labelled series.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "How to run and interpret",
      "type": "text"
    }
